{"content":[{"c":["REUEL"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Son of Esau by his wife Basemath, and the father of four sons: Nahath, Zerah, Shammah, and Mizzah (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.36.4,10-17","r":"Gen.36.4,10-17","rawR":"Gen.36.4,10-17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.36.4,10-17","value":"Gen.36.4,10-17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 36:4, 10-17"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Priest of Midian who gave his daughter to Moses for a wife. He is perhaps the same person as #1 above, and identical to Jethro (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.2.18","r":"Exod.2.18","rawR":"Exod.2.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.2.18","value":"Exod.2.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 2:18"},"; cf. ",{"href":"?bref=Exod.3.1","r":"Exod.3.1","rawR":"Exod.3.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.3.1","value":"Exod.3.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"3:1"},"). He is also called Raguel in ",{"href":"?bref=Num.10.29","r":"Num.10.29","rawR":"Num.10.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.10.29","value":"Num.10.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Numbers 10:29"}," (",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Jethro_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Jethro_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Jethro_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Jethro"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Alternate spelling of Deuel, Eliasaph’s father, in ",{"href":"?bref=Num.2.14","r":"Num.2.14","rawR":"Num.2.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.2.14","value":"Num.2.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Numbers 2:14"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Deuel_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Deuel_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Deuel_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Deuel"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Ancestor of Meshullam in Benjamin’s tribe (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.8","r":"1Chr.9.8","rawR":"1Chr.9.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.8","value":"1Chr.9.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 9:8"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":